{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBUPFc1WbuxPU1DGreb2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted index 1 (Fe 0.82 / Sb 0.18). It had the highest merit of the three compositions I measured, at an EQE of about 0.015%. That signal is very weak, and I can't tell whether it's the best in the library, because 27 of the 30 compositions were never measured.\n\n**What I measured (all 3 merit and all 5 XRD measurements used):**\n\n| Index | Fe / Sb | XRD | EQE |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 0.82 / 0.18 | not measured | **0.0147%** |\n| 20 | 0.31 / 0.69 | not measured (index 19 next to it showed a faint rutile peak) | -0.003% |\n| 24 | 0.21 / 0.79 | strongest rutile peaks | -0.004% |\n\n**How I got there:**\n- **XRD:** One strong peak set (Q ≈ 2.79, 3.22, 4.55, 5.33) appeared at every point I scanned (indices 4, 14, 19, 24, 29). That's probably the substrate. The only extra peaks, at Q ≈ 1.90 and 2.47, showed up in the Sb-rich films and were strongest at index 24. They fit a rutile FeSbO₄-type phase.\n- **Merit:** I spent my first two measurements on that rutile region (indices 24 and 20), and both came back at essentially zero. My best guess is that 2.1 eV light isn't absorbed well by the rutile phase, while Fe-rich, hematite-like films do absorb it. So I used the last measurement on the Fe-rich end.\n\nIndex 1 was a guess within the Fe-rich end. I picked it assuming a moderate amount of Sb helps the Fe oxide, but nothing I measured backs that up. Other Fe-rich compositions (indices 0–10) could well do better, and so could the middle of the line (indices 5–13), which got no merit measurements."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":451,"cache_read_input_tokens":9381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":451},"output_tokens":643,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo"